This repo has codex-setup-guide-offline.html: a self-contained setup guide
for Codex CLI on LM Windows laptops (Git Bash). It must stay one file with
inline CSS/JS, no CDN or web fonts, and no real credentials anywhere.

How it works: users paste NTID, EFOSS token, Genesis US and Global tokens
into step 2. Step 4 generates five downloads (combined.pem, tokens.txt,
bashrc.txt, npmrc.txt, config.toml), and step 5 is one command that backs up
existing files and moves them into ~ and ~/.codex. Tokens are never stored.
The cert gets pasted into the <script type="text/plain" id="lm-cert"> block.

Before changing anything, read the whole file. Then verify these against
my real setup and report back; don't edit yet:
1. The generated bashrc cert lines (NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS, SSL_CERT_FILE,
   REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE) vs. my ~/.bashrc.
2. Whether the openai-organization header on the US provider breaks
   gpt-oss-120b (it's there because the default model, gpt-5.6-terra, needs it).
3. The newest Sol model name for the codex-sol alias (gpt-5.6-sol vs gpt-6-sol).
4. That "codex -m X -c model_provider=aifactory_global" is valid on the
   installed Codex version (check codex -h).
